  StudySumTopic('lgs_ing.s45', 'lgs_ing', 'B2-3: A Balanced Life for Students', [
    ['Parça', 'Many students believe that success depends only on the number of hours spent studying. In fact, research suggests that quality matters more than quantity. A student who studies for two focused hours, takes short breaks and sleeps well will usually learn more than one who studies late into the night. Physical activity also improves concentration and mood. Similarly, spending time with friends and family helps to reduce stress. Of course, it is not easy to find a perfect balance, especially before important exams. Nevertheless, setting realistic goals, making a flexible schedule and asking for help when needed can make this period less stressful and more productive.'],
    ['Anahtar kelimeler (Tekrar et ile ekle)', 'balance = denge; quantity = nicelik; focused = odaklanmış; concentration = konsantrasyon; mood = ruh hali; stress = stres; realistic = gerçekçi; flexible = esnek; productive = verimli'],
    ['Soru 1', 'What matters more, quality or quantity? || Quality.'],
    ['Soru 2', 'How does physical activity help? || It improves concentration and mood.'],
    ['Soru 3', 'What can make the exam period less stressful? || Realistic goals, a flexible schedule and asking for help.'],
  ], grp: 'Okuma parçaları · B2'),
  StudySumTopic('lgs_ing.s46', 'lgs_ing', 'B2-4: The Power of Teamwork', [
    ['Parça', 'In the modern world, very few achievements are made by individuals alone. Space missions, medical research and even a simple school project depend on people working together. Good teamwork requires clear communication, trust and respect for different opinions. A team in which only one person talks and decides will probably miss valuable ideas. On the other hand, a team that shares responsibilities fairly and listens actively can solve complicated problems more quickly. Disagreements are natural; what matters is how they are handled. If members discuss them calmly and focus on the goal, conflict can even lead to better solutions. That is why employers value people who can cooperate.'],
    ['Anahtar kelimeler (Tekrar et ile ekle)', 'achievement = başarı; mission = görev; trust = güven; valuable = değerli; responsibility = sorumluluk; complicated = karmaşık; disagreement = anlaşmazlık; cooperate = işbirliği yapmak'],
    ['Soru 1', 'What does good teamwork require? || Clear communication, trust and respect.'],
    ['Soru 2', 'What happens when only one person decides? || The team may miss valuable ideas.'],
    ['Soru 3', 'Why do employers value cooperation? || Because teams solve problems better.'],
  ], grp: 'Okuma parçaları · B2'),
  StudySumTopic('lgs_ing.s0', 'lgs_ing', 'Ünite özetleri (8. sınıf)', [
    ['Ünite 1: Friendship', 'Davet etme, kabul etme ve reddetme; arkadaşlık ve planlama. Kalıplar: Would you like to ...? / I\'d love to, but ... / Let\'s ... / How about ...? / Sorry, I can\'t.'],
    ['Ünite 2: Teen Life', 'Gençlerin sosyal hayatı, görüş bildirme ve tavsiye verme. Kalıplar: In my opinion, ... / I think ... / You should ... / Why don\'t you ...?'],
    ['Ünite 3: In the Kitchen', 'Yemek tarifleri, mutfak malzemeleri ve sıralama. Sıralama bağlaçları: first, then, next, after that, finally. Ölçü: a cup of, a slice of, a pinch of.'],
    ['Ünite 4: On the Phone', 'Telefon konuşmaları, mesaj bırakma ve nezaketli ifadeler. Kalıplar: Can I speak to ...? / Hold on, please. / Can I take a message? / Could you call back later?'],
    ['Ünite 5: The Internet', 'İnternet kullanımı ve güvenlik; sosyal medya. Yapılar: should/shouldn\'t, must/mustn\'t, have to; tavsiye ve kural. Örnek: You shouldn\'t share your password.'],
    ['Ünite 6: Adventures', 'Macera ve doğa sporları; geçmişte yaşanmış olayları anlatma. Yapılar: Past Simple (V2) ve Past Continuous; bağlaçlar: when, while.'],
    ['Ünite 7: Tourism', 'Turist bilgileri, yer önerme ve karşılaştırma. Kalıplar: What\'s the best way to ...? / You can visit ... / It\'s famous for ... Karşılaştırma: -er than, more ... than, the -est, the most ...'],
    ['Ünite 8: Chores', 'Ev işleri ve sorumluluklar. Yapılar: have to / don\'t have to; mustn\'t; "do the dishes, take out the rubbish, make the bed, set the table, tidy up".'],
    ['Ünite 9: Science', 'Bilimsel buluşlar ve bilim insanları. Yapılar: Passive voice (is/are + V3, was/were + V3). Örnek: The telephone was invented by Alexander Graham Bell.'],
    ['Ünite 10: Natural Forces', 'Doğal afetler: earthquake, flood, tsunami, volcano, hurricane, drought. Yapılar: "will" ile tahmin; If clause (Type 1): If it rains, we will stay at home.'],
    ['Present Perfect özeti', 'Olumlu: S + have/has + V3. Olumsuz: haven\'t/hasn\'t + V3. Soru: Have/Has + S + V3? Örnek: She has visited London twice.'],
    ['Past Simple özeti', 'Olumlu: S + V2. Olumsuz: didn\'t + V1. Soru: Did + S + V1? Düzenli fiillere -ed gelir (played), düzensizler ezberlenir (went, saw, ate).'],
    ['Passive Voice özeti', 'Etken: The chef cooked the meal. Edilgen: The meal was cooked by the chef. Şimdiki zamanda: The room is cleaned every day.'],
    ['Conditionals (If clause Type 1)', 'If + Present Simple, will + V1. Örnek: If you study hard, you will pass the exam. Gerçekleşme olasılığı yüksek durumlar için.'],
